[
    {
        "content": "<p>I recently found it useful to give <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=measurable_from_top#doc\">docs#measurable_from_top</a> the <code>fun_prop</code> attribute, in order to automatically establish the measurability of a function of the form <code>x ↦ f ⌊x⌋₊</code> for some function <code>f</code> on the reals.  I'm thinking of submitting a PR to add this attribute, but I wanted to double check whether there were any potential downsides to doing so, and also whether this might also be an opportunity to look for similar <code>fun_prop</code> opportunities in the <code>MeasureTheory.MeasurableSpace.Basic</code> file.  My naive thought is that as long as there are no implicit arguments that might be tricky for <code>fun_prop</code> to infer, there is little harm in adding these tags, but perhaps there are some other considerations I should be aware of?</p>",
        "id": 606101589,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782250579
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>surely it's better to use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Measurable.of_discrete#doc\">docs#Measurable.of_discrete</a> instead?</p>",
        "id": 606110712,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782255082
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This doesn't seem to be sufficient.  Here is a MWE:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_discrete</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">measurable_from_top</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeeds</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here is the error message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"ss\">`fun_prop</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">was</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prove</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Issues</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">No</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theorems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Finset.sum</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">order</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prove</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">No</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theorems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Finset.sum</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">order</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prove</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Perhaps it is an instance diamond issue.</p>",
        "id": 606135636,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782268086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Measurable.from_top</code> lets <code>fun_prop</code> bypass the fact that there is no instance for <code>MeasurableSpace (Finset Nat)</code> by unifying the synthetic metavariable for the instance with <code>⊤</code>, this lets it decompose <code>fun (t : ℝ) ↦ ∑ n ∈ Finset.Ioc 0 ⌊t⌋₊, n</code> as <code>(fun t3 =&gt; ∑ n ∈ t3, n) ∘ (fun t4 =&gt; Finset.Ioc 0 t4) ∘ (fun t =&gt; ⌊t⌋₊)</code> which can all be shown to be measurable</p>",
        "id": 606137449,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782269350
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this doesn't seem like something <code>fun_prop</code> should be able to do</p>",
        "id": 606137674,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782269512
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, so this is the rare type of \"bug\" that actually makes the tactic <strong>more</strong> powerful (in some cases) rather than <strong>less</strong>?</p>",
        "id": 606137738,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782269546
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Giving <code>fun_prop</code> the ability to assign its own instances would seem to lead to an enormous amount of fruitless branching if there are no heuristics to limit what instances to select.</p>",
        "id": 606138133,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782269803
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this fails, for example</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">measurable_from_top</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeeds</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- note that there is currently not such an instance</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- failed to synthesize -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measurable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌊</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">⌋₊</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>because now that instance synthesis find an instance for <code>Finset Nat</code>, <code>fun_prop</code> can't use <code>⊤</code> as the instance</p>",
        "id": 606138330,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782269995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So this \"success\" of <code>fun_prop</code> is actually unwanted behavior because it is fragile to future implementation of instances for types that previously had no instance?</p>",
        "id": 606139122,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782270481
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The better fix would be to tag the lemma Aaron pointed and to endow <code>Finset X</code> with the sigma-algebra pulled back from that of <code>Set X</code> in the obvious way. The latter itself comes from the identification of <code>Set X</code> with <code>X -&gt; Prop</code>, where <code>Prop</code> has the discrete sigma-algebra.</p>",
        "id": 606247481,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1782308789
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, so what would one set <code>instance : Measurable (Finset Nat)</code> with in this case precisely?  And for the purpose of using it in a file to be upstreamed to Mathlib, should I set the instance to be private (if that is even possible) to avoid it being accidentally used elsewhere, or is there some canonical choice for this instance that is worth adding globally?</p>\n<p>The method <code>Measurable.of_discrete</code> is already tagged <code>fun_prop</code>, by the way, but I guess the issue was that <code>Finset Nat</code> didn't have a discrete structure.  (But <code>fun_prop</code> could theoretically have proven this measurability without such a structure by bypassing <code>Finset Nat</code> and going from <code>Nat</code> to <code>Real</code> directly, but I guess the metaprogramming somehow took a wrong turn.)</p>",
        "id": 606308730,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782322911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What I described above is the canonical instance (it's the smallest sigma-algebra making membership of each element measurable). It is a <em>theorem</em> that this results in the discrete sigma-algebra on <code>Finset Nat</code>. Concretely, you should provide <code>instance : MeasurableSpace (Finset X) := .comap SetLike.coe</code> and <code>instance :\nMeasurableSingletonClass (Finset X) := sorry</code>. Then <code>Measurable.of_discrete</code> will fire as expected on <code>Finset Nat</code> (which is <code>Countable</code>, so that <code>MeasurableSingletonClass</code> implies discreteness).</p>",
        "id": 606309975,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1782323198
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK.  Feels like overkill for this one application though (or more precisely, multiple applications in my file where I have a bunch of measurability conditions of this type to discharge).  One can also prove this measurability example by <code>Measurable.of_discrete (f := fun N ↦ ∑ n ∈ Finset.Ioc 0 N, n).comp Nat.measurable_floor</code> and avoid going through <code>Finset Nat</code> entirely.  It would be nice if <code>fun_prop</code> could be somehow nudged to go down this route.</p>",
        "id": 606311685,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782323661
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For what it is worth, I managed to create the instances with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instMeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SetLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">infer_instance</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Countable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSingletonClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">measurableSet_comap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Would these be instances that are worth adding to Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 606387643,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782357638
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes please!</p>",
        "id": 606400620,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1782366134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Now PR'ed at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41062\">#41062</a></p>",
        "id": 606622274,
        "sender_full_name": "Terence Tao",
        "timestamp": 1782440119
    }
]